+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` must turn schema-invalid tool calls into useful tool
+results, so a model can correct its call without ending the conversation.
+
+## Validation contract
+
+- `execute` validates input against the resolved definition's `inputSchema` before invoking the executor; a missing required property or wrong type returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing property and constraint, never its value, and does not invoke the executor. ([validated by: rejects invalid input safely before invoking the executor while preserving accepted input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L8))
+- Valid input is passed through unchanged, including schema-unlisted properties, and is executed exactly once. ([validated by: rejects invalid input safely before invoking the executor while preserving accepted input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L8))
+- An unknown tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>`. ([validated by: rejects invalid input safely before invoking the executor while preserving accepted input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L8))
+
+## Schema compilation
+
+- A static schema is compiled at registration time, and an uncompilable schema makes `register` throw a message naming the tool; a function-valued definition instead validates each call against the schema it resolves for that call. ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and resolves function schemas per call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L52))
+
+## Orchestrator integration
+
+- A validation failure is a tool result rather than an exception: the next tool-loop round receives the rejection text and can complete after a corrected retry. ([validated by: returns a schema rejection to the provider so its corrected retry resolves](../../src/orchestration/toolInputValidation.acceptance.test.ts#L15))
